{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>That we may bring the offering of HaShem.</b> In thought or in speech, and from here it follows that consecrated monetary value is called a קרבן (offering). <b>An anklet (אצעדה),</b> is a utensil for the leg with which one steps. <b>A bracelet (וצמיד),</b> is on the arm, and this is as it says (Genesis 24:22): ״ושני צמידים על ידיה״. <b>A ring (טבעת),</b> on the finger. <b>An earring (עגיל),</b> on the ear. <b>A capsule (וכומז),</b> a covering for the womb in the place of lewdness."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:27.677992838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}